>What corpses are dangerous/good to eat?
>What other way can u keep from starving to death?

Mild spoilers, 'cause I don't have a list handy:


Eat only fresh corpses.  Right after you kill it is safest.  Rotted
corpses will kill you unless you have a unicorn horn to apply to
yourself.  Zombie corpses and mummy corpses may be rotted right after
you kill them, so never eat them.

Some corpses are poisonous, so they'll damage you unless you're poison
resistant.  These include kobolds, giant spiders, and killer bees to
start.  Killer bees have a good chance of giving you poison resistance.
If you're still at the starving-to-death stage of the game, play 
barbarians, because they start with poison resistance.  (Even if you're
resistant, you'll get a message, so you'll get to know what's poisonous.)

Some corpses are acidic, and they'll damage you, too.  (You get a message
about a bad case of stomach acid.)  Generally, these are things like
acid blobs.  You'll figure out what's what eventually.

Eating bats will stun you for a few turns, and some things like
violet fungus may make you hallucinate if you eat them.  A pain.  Get
a unicorn horn.

Good things to eat include jackals, rothes, floating eyes (telepathy),
killer bees (poison resistance), orcs, hobbits, gnomes, elves (sleep
resistance; don't eat them if you're an elf because of cannibalism),
dragons (fat chance of killing one early), ...

Don't eat humans or cats or dogs.  (Tigers and wolves and stuff are fine,
just not regular pets.)

If you're fainting from lack of food or about to die from other causes,
pray.  As a new player, only pray in emergencies -- it's not unlimited,
so save it until you need it.

Also, don't hang around in one place too long unless you've got lots 
of food.  Press on downward, as long as you're healed.  Just watch
the status line and know when to run away.

